  "published": "2026-10-25T06:52:23.033Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.6.4: fixed the native loader crashing on Android instead of loading the library. AppContext.BaseDirectory is an empty string on .NET for Android and was passed straight to DirectoryInfo, so the first call into HCVault.Core died with ArgumentException: The value cannot be an empty string (Parameter 'path') before any load was attempted - the library could never be used from an Android app. Directory probing is now best effort (a host without an application directory simply contributes no candidates), Android asks the platform loader by name first (the .so lives inside the APK at lib/{abi}/), and a failure there reports the missing ABI together with the exact RuntimeIdentifiers / AndroidNativeLibrary fix - emulators are x86_64 while phones are arm64-v8a, which is the usual cause. The report also lists the app's real native library directory and what was packaged into it, so 'the .so never shipped' is distinguishable from 'it shipped but the OS refused it' at a glance. Hosts that publish no runtime identifier (Android reports 'unknown') now derive one from the process architecture instead of probing a runtimes/unknown/ path. No API changes; the native library is unchanged (vcapi v6).",
